  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining the Expansion of the Overseas Health Assessment and Management of U.S. - Bound Refugees, Non-Immigrant Visa Applicants and other Migrant Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to ensure that refugees assisted by IOM within the US Refugee Admissions Program (USRAP) arrive to the United States vaccinated and thus protected against many of the common vaccine preventable diseases. At the central level, the project will be managed by IOM under technical guidance from Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. Logistical support of vaccine procurement and delivery to the IOM field offices is expected to be organized in partnership with international and private sector service providers. At the field level, IOM missions will implement the project in partnership with the ministries of health and other agencies involved in the immunization activities.</narrative>
  </description>
